=== real QM: are rho_+ and rho_- distinguishable by LOCAL statistics? ===
  without references (A | B only): 0.0
  references in the shared real state (|01>-|10>)/sqrt2: <J (x) J>_ref = +1.000; max local-statistics difference = 2.000
  references in a product state |00>: <J (x) J>_ref = +0.000; max local-statistics difference = 0.000
  references maximally mixed: max local-statistics difference = 0.000

=== ABW-type encoding: complex QM = real QM + one GLOBAL reference rebit ===
  <psi|A|psi> complex = -3.454168;  real encoding = -3.454168;  A_R symmetric: True
  -> the imaginary unit is a physical, globally shared reference rebit; local tomography holds exactly when every
     party has (correlated) access to that frame. LT is therefore a property of a SHARED REFERENCE STATE (C5-H),
     not of the single-system kinematics.
